Done. Here's a summary of what was created:

**T1 — Scaffold**
- `package.json` — `type: module`, scripts `dev/build/preview/test/lint`
- `tsconfig.json` — strict, `moduleResolution: bundler`
- `vite.config.ts` — base `/dead-phone-directory/`
- `vitest.config.ts` — node environment, `src/lib/**` only
- `eslint.config.js` — typescript-eslint + `no-restricted-globals` blocking `window`/`document`/`localStorage` in `src/lib/`
- `index.html` — `<header>`, `<nav>`, four `<section>` elements, `<footer>`
- `public/manifest.json` — name, short_name, display: standalone
- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` — build → `upload-pages-artifact` → `deploy-pages`
- All 6 deps installed via `npm install --save-dev --no-audit --no-fund`

**T2 — `phone.ts`**
- `isServiceNumber` — `/^[2-9]11$/` or `"988"`
- `normalise` — strips formatting, validates NANP area/exchange codes, accepts 3/10/11-digit
- `format` — `(NXX) NXX-XXXX` / `1 (NXX) NXX-XXXX` / pass-through for service numbers
- 36 tests: unit cases covering all formats, rejection paths, plus P1–P4 property tests

**T3 — `scheduler.ts`**
- `intervalDays` — `2^(box-1)`
- `recordCorrect` — advances box (capped at 5), due = today + interval; UTC day math avoids DST bugs
- `recordIncorrect` — resets to box 1, due = today
- `isDue` — lexicographic ISO comparison
- 25 tests: all box transitions, month/year/leap-day rollovers, boundary dates, plus P5–P8 property tests

**Results: 61 tests passed, lint clean.**
